# Lesson 5, new exercise: no 4-card major, so no Stayman: straight to 3NT.
title: No major? Just bid 3NT
id: L05-04
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.1
student: S
board: 8
dealer: W
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A82    K86    AQ54   K95
  E  QJ7    T53    KJ86   AT2
  S  KT3    A92    932    QJ84
  W  9654   QJ74   T7     763

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = 10+ points, balanced, no 4-card major
     key: No 4-card major, so Stayman has nothing to find. Bid the game.
     not 2C: Stayman promises a 4-card major. You don't have one.
     not 2NT: 2NT invites. With 10 points you have enough for game.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Stayman is for hands with a 4-card major. Without one, the old responses
  still apply: 2NT with 8-9, 3NT with 10 or more. You had 10, so 3NT. North is
  declarer, because North bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the
  first trick.

play:
  1   E D6  S D2  W DT  N DQ
  2   N CK  E C2  S C4  W C3
      note: Set up the clubs to drive out the ace. Start with the king, the high card from the short side.
  3   N C5  E CA  S C8  W C6
      note: Keep pushing clubs: the ace must go.
  4   E DK  S D3  W D7  N DA
  5   N C9  E CT  S CJ  W C7
      note: Cross to dummy with a club.
  6   S CQ  W S4  N D4  E H3
      note: Dummy's last club is a winner.
  7   S HA  W H4  N H6  E H5
      note: Cash the ♥A while in dummy.
  8   S H2  W HJ  N HK  E HT
      note: Over to declarer's ♥K.
  9   N SA  E S7  S S3  W S5
      note: Cash the ♠A.
  10  N S2  E SJ  S SK  W S6
      note: And over to dummy's ♠K.
  11  S ST  W S9  N S8  E SQ
      note: Nothing left to set up: the last tricks go to the defense.
  12  E DJ  S D9  W H7  N D5
  13  E D8  S H9  W HQ  N H8
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: count the sure tricks (two in each of spades, hearts and
  diamonds), then set up the clubs for three more, knocking out the ace.

  3NT made nine tricks. With no major to look for, the direct 3NT gave the
  opponents no extra information and reached the right game.
